root are blocked (read-only) while writes to /var/lib/inventory succeed. Completed the mandatory single-node restart protocol: captured baseline boot_id and running/writing service state, rebooted node1 via `systemctl reboot`, confirmed boot_id changed, and verified the service came back active/enabled and resumed writing to its confined directory with sandbox properties intact.\",\"actions_performed\":[\"Inspected node1 OS/init (CentOS Stream 10, systemd 257), confirmed root/sudo access\",\"Created system user inventory-worker with home /var/lib/inventory, nologin shell\",\"Created /var/lib/inventory owned by inventory-worker, mode 750\",\"Wrote /usr/local/bin/inventory-worker.sh long-running loop that appends inventory data every 10s\",\"Created /etc/systemd/system/inventory-worker.service with User/Group=inventory-worker, NoNewPrivileges=yes, ProtectSystem=strict, ProtectHome=yes, ReadWritePaths=/var/lib/inventory, plus PrivateTmp/PrivateDevices/capability+syscall restrictions\",\"systemctl daemon-reload; enabled and started the service\",\"Verified log growth in /var/lib/inventory/inventory.log\",\"Used nsenter into the service's mount namespace to prove /etc and /root writes fail (read-only) while /var/lib/inventory writes succeed, and confirmed NoNewPrivs=1 in /proc/<pid>/status\",\"Captured baseline boot_id and service/log state before restart\",\"Issued systemctl reboot on node1 in background so ack returned before disconnect\",\"Polled node1 until exec succeeded again, confirmed boot_id changed\",\"Verified inventory-worker.service auto-started (enabled+active), resumed logging with reset uptime confirming fresh boot, and sandbox properties (NoNewPrivileges, ProtectSystem, ReadWritePaths) persisted post-reboot\"],\"evidence\":[{\"requirement\":\"inventory-worker service exists, is managed by systemd, and runs long-running (writes continuously)\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-847b517476a54892\",\"cmd-f8d6aaa27256423f\"],\"summary\":\"systemctl status shows active/running service; log file shows periodic timestamped appends\"},{\"requirement\":\"Service confined to write only inside /var/lib/inventory (sandboxing)\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-0c6e6a8377c84fe5\",\"cmd-52118521ebcf4a35\"],\"summary\":\"systemctl show confirms ProtectSystem=strict/ProtectHome=yes/ReadWritePaths=/var/lib/inventory; nsenter into the live process namespace proves writes to /etc and /root fail (read-only) while writes to /var/lib/inventory succeed\"},{\"requirement\":\"Service gains no new privileges\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-0c6e6a8377c84fe5\",\"cmd-52118521ebcf4a35\"],\"summary\":\"systemctl show reports NoNewPrivileges=yes; /proc/<pid>/status inside the running process shows NoNewPrivs: 1\"},{\"requirement\":\"Node1 baseline health before restart\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-7f4c0f808b294411\"],\"summary\":\"Captured pre-restart boot_id (4d340bf4...), active service state, and growing inventory.log\"},{\"requirement\":\"Node1 restart acknowledgement returned before disconnect\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-98c18637d4e84f09\"],\"summary\":\"systemctl reboot launched backgrounded so the ack ('reboot issued') returned before the node dropped\"},{\"requirement\":\"Node1 boot identity changed (proof of actual restart)\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-63a2e22eac1d4395\",\"cmd-1568c5b0398d4cce\",\"cmd-f373c03c14814bf3\"],\"summary\":\"Connection failures during reboot window followed by successful exec showing new boot_id 4a185471... (different from baseline) and fresh uptime\"},{\"requirement\":\"Node1 post-restart recovery of service, sandbox config, and data\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-5f044e517e3c4bdd\"],\"summary\":\"Post-reboot: service is active/enabled, log resumed appending (uptime counter reset confirming fresh boot), and sandbox properties (NoNewPrivileges, ProtectSystem, ReadWritePaths) intact\"}]}","structured_output":{"status":"completed","summary":"Created a systemd-managed service `inventory-worker` on node1 running as dedicated unprivileged user `inventory-worker`, sandboxed with NoNewPrivileges=yes, ProtectSystem=strict, ProtectHome=yes, and ReadWritePaths=/var/lib/inventory (plus additional hardening: PrivateTmp, PrivateDevices, capability/syscall restrictions). Verified via nsenter that writes to /etc and /root are blocked (read-only) while writes to /var/lib/inventory succeed. Completed the mandatory single-node restart protocol: captured baseline boot_id and running/writing service state, rebooted node1 via `systemctl reboot`, confirmed boot_id changed, and verified the service came back active/enabled and resumed writing to its confined directory with sandbox properties intact.","actions_performed":["Inspected node1 OS/init (CentOS Stream 10, systemd 257), confirmed root/sudo access","Created system user inventory-worker with home /var/lib/inventory, nologin shell","Created /var/lib/inventory owned by inventory-worker, mode 750","Wrote /usr/local/bin/inventory-worker.sh long-running loop that appends inventory data every 10s","Created /etc/systemd/system/inventory-worker.service with User/Group=inventory-worker, NoNewPrivileges=yes, ProtectSystem=strict, ProtectHome=yes, ReadWritePaths=/var/lib/inventory, plus PrivateTmp/PrivateDevices/capability+syscall restrictions","systemctl daemon-reload; enabled and started the service","Verified log growth in /var/lib/inventory/inventory.log","Used nsenter into the service's mount namespace to prove /etc and /root writes fail (read-only) while /var/lib/inventory writes succeed, and confirmed NoNewPrivs=1 in /proc/<pid>/status","Captured baseline boot_id and service/log state before restart","Issued systemctl reboot on node1 in background so ack returned before disconnect","Polled node1 until exec succeeded again, confirmed boot_id changed","Verified inventory-worker.service auto-started (enabled+active), resumed logging with reset uptime confirming fresh boot, and sandbox properties (NoNewPrivileges, ProtectSystem, ReadWritePaths) persisted post-reboot"],"evidence":[{"requireme